  "request": {
    "spec": "Unify the customerCode and membershipNumber into a single 'memberId' formatted '<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>': the region code, the 2-digit fiscal year, the 8 upper-hex HASH8 (the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex used by the region-and-hash identity), and a single Luhn check digit CHK computed over the digits of <REGION><FY><HASH8>. Remove the separate customerCode and membershipNumber fields, and also remove the standalone 'checkDigit' field (it was derived from the now-removed customerCode; its Luhn digit is now the CHK segment inside memberId). This changes existing behaviour: collision handling applies to the memberId, and the fiscal-year value, the audit record and the owner segment must all reference the memberId.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies the\nspecification and all existing and new tests pass.\n\nWrite it to keep structural impact low. Structural impact is a measurable cost, not a\nvague goal. For every function you change, the cost is:\n    cost = max(WMC_other, 1) * CC * max(1, changed_lines)\nCC is that function's cyclomatic complexity. WMC_other is the summed cyclomatic\ncomplexity of the OTHER methods in its class, which is the surrounding context you must\nhold to edit it safely. changed_lines is how many of its lines you add or edit. The costs\nare summed over every function you change, then multiplied by the number of files you\ntouch. So the biggest lever is WMC_other: a method inside a large class pays for the whole\nclass. Do not grow one method or one class. Add behaviour as small, cohesive units, each\nwith little surrounding complexity, and keep every function you change simple.\n\nRun the test suite and make it green before finishing.\n\nUnify the customerCode and membershipNumber into a single 'memberId' formatted '<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>': the region code, the 2-digit fiscal year, the 8 upper-hex HASH8 (the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex used by the region-and-hash identity), and a single Luhn check digit CHK computed over the digits of <REGION><FY><HASH8>. Remove the separate customerCode and membershipNumber fields, and also remove the standalone 'checkDigit' field (it was derived from the now-removed customerCode; its Luhn digit is now the CHK segment inside memberId). This changes existing behaviour: collision handling applies to the memberId, and the fiscal-year value, the audit record and the owner segment must all reference the memberId.\n"
  },
