    "result_text": "Full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nUnified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. Example produced by the run: `NSW26 16E6609E 3` \u2192 region `NSW`, fiscal year `26`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, Luhn check `3`.\n\nFiles touched (6), each kept minimal:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed the `customerCode` field/column/getter/setter to `memberId` (column `member_id`). Two one-line accessors changed.\n2. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (the test DB uses `ddl-auto=none`; h2 uses `update`).\n3. **`rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now builds `region + FY(2-digit) + HASH8`, appends the Luhn `CHK` over that prefix (reusing the existing `CheckDigit` helper), then runs the same collision loop against existing owners' `memberId`s. The hash and collision logic are unchanged in shape.\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings and the now-dead `membershipNumber()` default method. `memberId` maps by name automatically.\n5. **`rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the two audit records now reference `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single read-only `memberId`.\n\nThe fiscal year, the audit record, the owner segment (unchanged, already region-based), and collision handling all now key off `memberId`. I kept the derivation inside the small existing single-method step classes rather than growing any function or touching the large mapper's other logic, and left the class name `AssignCustomerCode` in place to avoid re-wiring the POST pipeline YAML.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: I left the step class named `AssignCustomerCode` (its body now assigns `memberId`) to avoid touching `owners.POST.yml` and keep structural impact down. If you'd prefer the class renamed to `AssignMemberId` for clarity, that's a one-file-plus-YAML follow-up.",
